    <statement><p>Consider <m>\displaystyle \mbox{div}\,\left(\frac{-y\vec i + x\vec j}{(x^2 + y^2)^{2}}\right)</m>.</p>
<p><alert>(a)</alert>
Is this a vector or a scalar?  <ul form="popup" name="AnSwEr0001"><li>
<p>?</p>
</li><li>
<p>vector</p>
</li><li>
<p>scalar</p>
</li></ul></p>
<p><alert>(b)</alert>
Calculate it:</p>
<p><m>\mbox{div}\,\left(\frac{-y\vec i + x\vec j}{(x^2 + y^2)^{2}}\right) =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/> + <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/> = <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\text{scalar}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{2\cdot 2xy}{\left(x^{2}+y^{2}\right)^{2+1}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{-2\cdot 2xy}{\left(x^{2}+y^{2}\right)^{2+1}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert>(a)</alert>
<m>\mbox{div}\,\left(\frac{-y\vec i + x\vec j}{(x^2 + y^2)^{2}}\right)</m> is a scalar




<alert>(b)</alert>
We have
<me>\mbox{div}\,\left(\frac{-y\vec i + x\vec j}{(x^2 + y^2)^{2}}\right) = \frac{4xy}{\left(x^{2}+y^{2}\right)^{3}} + \frac{-4xy}{\left(x^{2}+y^{2}\right)^{3}} = 0.</me>



</solution>
